Training Rollout
National trainers’ roles
National trainers will be determined from the relevant regulatory bodies. Their roles will be to:
1. Develop training content using national standardised training guidelines and curriculum;
2. Train ToTs from the county level;
3. Give oversight to the ToT training at the county level.
County Level
1. Train health care providers in the county level facilities (levels 2 to 6);
2. Supervision of trainees.
